<details>
<summary>Trace evidence from UCX 1.21.0</summary>

Run with a logging-enabled UCX build:

```bash
UCX_TLS=tcp,cuda_copy,cuda_ipc UCX_RNDV_FRAG_MEM_TYPES=cuda \
UCX_LOG_LEVEL=trace UCX_LOG_FILE=ucx-trace-%p.log \
  ./ucx_same_process_cuda_ipc_oom --iterations 1 --warmup 0
```

Relevant trace excerpt:

```text
rendezvous data fetch into cuda-managed memory from cuda
mpool ucp_rndv_frags: align 1, maxelems 4294967295, elemsize 24
could not allocate ucp_rndv_frags: cuda memory length=536870912 flags=0x364 num_methods=1
mpool ucp_rndv_frags: allocated chunk ... with 128 elements
```

`536870912` bytes is 512 MiB, matching the default CUDA fragment allocation count and fragment size.

</details>

